{"id":"uzzah","name":"Uzzah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:uzzah"],"groups":["1. Also called UZZA, son of Abinadab"],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Uzzah","text":"Strength, a son of Abinadab, in whose house the men of Kirjath-jearim placed the ark when it was brought back from the land of the Philistines (1 Sam. 7:1). He with his brother Ahio drove the cart on which the ark was placed when David sought to bring it up to Jerusalem. When the oxen stumbled, Uzzah, in direct violation of the divine law (Num. 4:15), put forth his hand to steady the ark, and was immediately smitten unto death. The place where this occurred was henceforth called Perez-uzzah (1 Chr. 13:11). David on this feared to proceed further, and placed the ark in the house of Obed-edom the Gittite (2 Sam. 6:2-11; 1 Chr. 13:6-13)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5798","lemma":"עֻזָּא","xlit":"ʻUzzâʼ","gloss":"Uzza or Uzzah, the name of five Israelites","kjv":"Uzza, Uzzah","count":8,"share":1},{"strong":"H727","lemma":"אָרוֹן","xlit":"ʼârôwn","gloss":"a box","kjv":"ark, chest, coffin","count":6,"share":0.75},{"strong":"H2734","lemma":"חָרָה","xlit":"chârâh","gloss":"to glow or grow warm","kjv":"be angry, burn, be displeased, earnestly","count":4,"share":0.5},{"strong":"H6560","lemma":"פֶּרֶץ עֻזָּא","xlit":"Perets ʻUzzâʼ","gloss":"Perets-Uzza, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Perezuzza","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H283","lemma":"אַחְיוֹ","xlit":"ʼAchyôw","gloss":"Achio, the name of three Israelites","kjv":"Ahio","count":2,"share":0.25},{"strong":"H8058","lemma":"שָׁמַט","xlit":"shâmaṭ","gloss":"to fling down","kjv":"discontinue, overthrow, release, let rest","count":2,"share":0.25}],"verses":["2Sam.6.3","2Sam.6.6","2Sam.6.7","2Sam.6.8","1Chr.13.7","1Chr.13.9","1Chr.13.10","1Chr.13.11"],"related":[{"id":"nachon","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.375,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"kirjath-jearim","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.172,"why":"5 ver